      "observations": [
        "Snapshot encryption/MAC keys use a different service/account and code path from rejoin credentials. Exactly 64 random bytes split into independent AES-256 and HMAC-SHA256 keys.",
        "Snapshot key first-create handles duplicate add by re-reading the durable winner; candidate keys are zeroed. Decrypt authenticates header, filename, IV and ciphertext before decrypting.",
        "Files are atomically installed under Application Support with complete Data Protection and backup exclusion; reads are bounded at maximum+1. Plaintext max=8MiB.",
        "Legacy Documents directory is excluded before list/read. Malformed or failed migration records remain addressable and last copies are retained; protected-record precedence is not bypassed. Exclusion failures propagate outside best-effort per-record migration.",
        "Snapshot list on a fresh empty store need not invoke SnapshotKeychain. Exceptions are kept distinct from NotFound; raw platform errors do not enter UI state."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Credential OSStatus traces cannot be attributed to snapshot Keychain operations. Snapshot numeric attribution remains false in native controls.",
        "Synthetic .native-readiness filename can test I/O boundaries but is not an ordinary session snapshot filename or complete game-resume proof.",
        "Simulator filesystem attributes do not prove hardware lock/unlock, backup, or authenticated signed-release behavior."
