      "observations": [
        "Settings mutations use app-owned scope; per-setting update writes to backing before flow emission, serialized by one mutex. A platform write accepted by NSUserDefaults is not a durable flush.",
        "Locale owner reads the application persistent domain, never promotes resolved fallback. It records prior state before installation, and restores only when the current value exactly matches the installed value. Unowned/external preferences remain authoritative.",
        "System releases the previous owned value even after process death; an already-identical OS preference is not claimed or later removed. Malformed ownership cannot install malformed previous arrays.",
        "Composition boundary is not keyed by locale. AppScope, navigator and retained state are not intentionally recreated by language changes. Native semantic direction is refreshed only on actual direction changes; SwiftUI update retains same container and child."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "NSUserDefaults commits in-process immediately and to disk asynchronously. The source does not promise a cross-process transaction or crash-proof durability across every interruption.",
        "Synthetic suite tests cannot prove actual OS per-app language representation. Native matrix must exercise an OS-created PRESENT Arabic preference (with global English), English override, System, and restart. ABSENT does not count as PRESENT.",
        "Actual iOS gesture correctness and real OS persistence require runtime evidence. No iOS tests were launched by this reviewer in this cycle."
      ]
